-- Behaviour-oriented concurrency (Cheeseman et al., OOPSLA 2023) over a
-- typed store: the store is one value, of a shape the program declares
-- (`(Int, Int, List String)`), and a cown is a position in it
-- (`Cown s a`, an `a` in an `s`: std.store's).  `when c body` spawns a
-- behaviour: later, once, with every cown of `c` its own at once, it is
-- given what they hold and gives back what they are to hold after it.
-- Behaviours whose cowns overlap run one after another, in the order
-- they were spawned; the others run as they come, among green threads.
-- A behaviour takes its cowns all at once, never one and then another,
-- so behaviours do not deadlock on them.
--
-- > [!CAUTION]
-- > Unstable: concurrency in heff is not settled. What this module offers
-- > may change, or go, in any release.
--
-- ```haskell
-- import co
-- import green
-- import std.boc
-- import std.store
--
-- type Bank = (Int, Int, List String)
--
-- alice : Cown Bank Int
-- alice = first
--
-- bob : Cown Bank Int
-- bob = second
--
-- moves : Cown Bank (List String)
-- moves = third
--
-- -- | `n` moved from alice to bob, where she has it, and said so: one
-- -- | behaviour on all three
-- paid : {e : HFunctor} -> {{gr : green <: e}} -> {{bc : boc Bank <: e}} -> Int -> Co e Unit
-- paid n =
--   when (alice, bob, moves) (\(a, b, ms) ->
--     if a >= n then pure (a - n, b + n, ("paid " ^ show n) :: ms)
--     else pure (a, b, ms))
--
-- -- | alice given 10, then 5 paid, on a store of nothing yet: what bob
-- -- | has at the end, `Just 5`
-- run : Maybe Int
-- run =
--   case runBoc (0, 0, Nil) (do
--     when alice (\a -> pure (a + 10))
--     paid 5) of
--     Just (u, end) -> Just (contents bob end)
--     Nothing -> Nothing
-- ```
--
-- Operation | What it does
-- --- | ---
-- `when c body` | a behaviour spawned on the cown `c`, or a tuple of them; this one goes on
-- `whenever c cond body` | ... that runs once `cond` holds of what they hold, waiting for a write until it does
-- `drained` | waits until no behaviour is left to run
-- `runBoc st c` | `c` and its behaviours run on the store `st`, in the language
-- `steps bs` | how many steps the queues of the behaviours `bs` have taken
--
-- A behaviour's body is given what its cowns hold, a tuple as the cowns
-- are (`(a, b, log)` hands it an `(x, y, l)`, nesting to the left), and
-- gives back their new contents, the same shape: `Cowns` says what a
-- cown or a tuple of them holds.  The body is a
-- computation of the world like any other: it may spawn behaviours, on
-- its own cowns too (they run after it), and nothing stops it doing
-- what else its effects allow.  But a body that waits -- `recv` on a
-- channel, a behaviour's end it hopes for -- holds its cowns while it
-- waits, and every behaviour behind it on them waits too; where every
-- thread waits, the scheduler says so (`runBoc`'s `Nothing`).
--
-- The cowns of one `when` are apart: the same cown twice, or one inside
-- another (`whole` and `first`), is abandoned when the `when` runs.
-- Cowns of two behaviours may be one inside the other: the two overlap.
--
-- Each part of the store a behaviour is on has a queue, as each cown
-- has in the paper: a behaviour comes to the queue of each of its cowns
-- at once when it is spawned, and to the queue of each part they are
-- inside, for a part inside it (behaviours for parts inside one part do
-- not wait for each other there, but one for all of it waits for them,
-- and they for it).  It counts the queues it waits in, and its turn
-- comes when none is left; when it ends, only the queues it was in are
-- looked at, their fronts let in.  So a behaviour costs as many steps as
-- it has parts (`steps`), however many others wait.
--
-- `whenever c cond body` is a conditional critical region (Hoare's and
-- Brinch Hansen's, 1972) over cowns, as std.stm's `check` is over
-- transactional variables.  Its turn comes as a `when`'s does; where
-- `cond` does not hold of what its cowns hold then, it lets them go,
-- having written nothing, and waits, taking no turn, until another
-- behaviour that has one of them -- or a part inside one, or one they
-- are inside -- ends, which writes them.  Then it comes to their queues
-- again, at the back, those woken by one write in the order they were
-- spawned, and tries again.  A behaviour that gives up writes nothing,
-- so two waiting do not wake each other: where every behaviour left
-- waits so, nothing is left to write, and `runBoc` says every thread
-- waits (`Nothing`), as std.stm's `runGreen` does.  It comes back at
-- the back, not where it was, for a place among behaviours already let
-- in at some of their cowns could close a cycle: it is never passed by
-- a behaviour spawned after the write that woke it, but one before it
-- may make `cond` false again.
--
-- Behaviours are green threads, the store and the queue of behaviours
-- the world's state (`boc s`, handled in the language, as std.state's
-- `runState` does).  `runBoc` runs a program and its behaviours on a
-- store and nothing else, waiting for the last behaviour before it
-- answers, on every backend.  A program of the world handles `boc s`
-- itself, `runState (opening st)` around green's `scheduled`, and waits
-- for `drained` before it reads the store.

module std.boc
  ( Cown
  , Cowns
  , instanceCownsPosition
  , instanceCownsPair
  , Behaviours
  , boc
  , when
  , whenever
  , drained
  , opening
  , steps
  , runBoc
  )

import co
import green
import state
import std.ordmap as OrdMap
import std.store

-- | A cown holding an `a`, in a store of shape `s`: a position in it.
type Cown s a = Position s a

-- The queues
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (a behaviour waiting in a part's queue: its key, and whether it is for
-- all of the part, or for a part inside it)
type Entry = { key : Int, here : Bool }

-- (a part of the store, as behaviours have it: whether one holds all of
-- it; how many hold parts inside it; those waiting for it, in the order
-- they came; and the keys of those waiting until it is written, on all
-- of it, and on a part inside it)
type Slot =
  { held : Bool
  , within : Int
  , queue : Queue Entry
  , watchedHere : OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit
  , watchedWithin : OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit
  }

-- (a behaviour not yet done: how many of its parts' queues it still
-- waits in, and its parts, each whether it is for all of it -- its
-- cowns' own -- or for a part inside it)
type Waiting = { left : Int, nodes : List (Pair Part Bool) }

-- (the queue of each part behaviours are on, the behaviours not yet
-- done by their keys, and how many steps the queues have taken)
type Queues =
  { slots : OrdMap.OrdMap Part Slot
  , waiting : OrdMap.OrdMap Int Waiting
  , taken : Int
  }

-- | The store behaviours share; the queues of its parts and the
-- | behaviours waiting in them; how many behaviours are not yet done;
-- | and the keys of those waiting until none is left.
type Behaviours s = { now : s, queues : Queues, live : Int, idle : List Int }

-- | ... as the world's state.
boc : Type -> HFunctor
boc s = state (Behaviours s)

-- | The store `st`, no behaviour spawned.
opening : {s : Type} -> s -> Behaviours s
opening st =
  { now = st
  , queues = { slots = OrdMap.empty, waiting = OrdMap.empty, taken = 0 }
  , live = 0
  , idle = Nil
  }

-- | How many steps the queues have taken, from `opening` on: a
-- | behaviour's coming to a part's queue, its being let in there, its
-- | leaving, its waiting for a write and being woken by one.  What
-- | behaviours cost to schedule, as many for each as it has parts,
-- | however many others wait.
steps : {s : Type} -> Behaviours s -> Int
steps bs = bs.queues.taken

-- (none of the parts overlaps another)
apart : List Part -> Bool
apart Nil = True
apart (p :: ps) = not (List.any (\q -> overlaps p q) ps) && apart ps

-- (the part, for all of it, and the parts it is inside, for a part
-- inside them)
withEnclosing : OrdMap.OrdMap Part Bool -> Part -> OrdMap.OrdMap Part Bool
withEnclosing m p =
  OrdMap.insert
    (List.foldl (\n q -> OrdMap.insert n q False) m (enclosing p))
    p
    True

-- (the queues a behaviour on the parts waits in: each of its parts, for
-- all of it, and each part those are inside, for a part inside it, once
-- each; of parts apart, none is inside another)
nodesOf : List Part -> List (Pair Part Bool)
nodesOf ps = OrdMap.toList (List.foldl withEnclosing OrdMap.empty ps)

-- (a part no behaviour is on)
emptySlot : Slot
emptySlot =
  { held = False
  , within = 0
  , queue = emptyQ
  , watchedHere = OrdMap.empty
  , watchedWithin = OrdMap.empty
  }

-- (none)
noKeys : OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit -> Bool
noKeys m = case OrdMap.findMin m of
  Just kv -> False
  Nothing -> True

-- (nothing held, waiting or watching)
unused : Slot -> Bool
unused sl =
  not sl.held
  && sl.within == 0
  && isEmptyQ sl.queue
  && noKeys sl.watchedHere
  && noKeys sl.watchedWithin

slotOf : Queues -> Part -> Slot
slotOf qs p = fromMaybe emptySlot (OrdMap.lookup qs.slots p)

-- (... the part's slot `sl` now, `n` steps taken; a slot no behaviour
-- is on let go of)
withSlot : Queues -> Part -> Slot -> Int -> Queues
withSlot qs p sl n =
  { qs
  | slots =
      if unused sl then OrdMap.delete qs.slots p
      else OrdMap.insert qs.slots p sl
  , taken = qs.taken + n
  }

-- (whether a behaviour can be let in at the part now: for all of it,
-- where none holds any of it; for a part inside it, where none holds
-- all of it)
fits : Slot -> Bool -> Bool
fits sl True = not sl.held && sl.within == 0
fits sl False = not sl.held

-- (... let in)
granted : Slot -> Bool -> Slot
granted sl True = { sl | held = True }
granted sl False = { sl | within = sl.within + 1 }

-- (... gone)
released : Slot -> Bool -> Slot
released sl True = { sl | held = False }
released sl False = { sl | within = sl.within - 1 }

-- (the behaviour `k` come to the part's queue: let in at once, where
-- none waits before it and it fits; else at the back, waiting)
joined : Int -> Bool -> Slot -> Pair Slot Bool
joined k here sl =
  if isEmptyQ sl.queue && fits sl here then MkPair (granted sl here) False
  else MkPair { sl | queue = putQ { key = k, here = here } sl.queue } True

-- (those at the front of the part's queue that fit, let in, in turn:
-- one for all of it, or those for parts inside it up to the next for
-- all; the slot after, its queue's front turned round once, and their
-- keys, `ks` those let in so far)
letIn : Slot -> List Int -> Pair Slot (List Int)
letIn sl ks = case takeQ sl.queue of
  Just (MkPair en rest) ->
    if fits sl en.here
    then letIn (granted { sl | queue = rest } en.here) (en.key :: ks)
    else MkPair
        { sl | queue = { rest | front = en :: rest.front } }
        (List.reverse ks)
  Nothing -> MkPair sl (List.reverse ks)

-- (the behaviour `k` come to each of its parts' queues, `n` those it
-- waits in so far: the queues after, and in how many it waits)
joinedAll : Int -> List (Pair Part Bool) -> Int -> Queues -> Pair Queues Int
joinedAll k Nil n qs = MkPair qs n
joinedAll k (MkPair p here :: rest) n qs =
  let (sl, waits) = joined k here (slotOf qs p)
  in joinedAll k rest (if waits then n + 1 else n) (withSlot qs p sl 1)

-- (the behaviour `k` waiting so)
waitingIn : Int -> Waiting -> Queues -> Queues
waitingIn k w qs = { qs | waiting = OrdMap.insert qs.waiting k w }

-- (... and so waiting, or, waiting in none, let in: whether it was)
queuedAs : Int -> List (Pair Part Bool) -> Queues -> Pair Queues Bool
queuedAs k nodes qs =
  let (after, n) = joinedAll k nodes 0 qs
  in MkPair (waitingIn k { left = n, nodes = nodes } after) (n == 0)

-- (the behaviours `ks` each let in at one more of its parts: the queues
-- after, and `woken` with those let in at the last of theirs, to be
-- woken)
counted : Queues -> List Int -> List Int -> Pair Queues (List Int)
counted qs Nil woken = MkPair qs woken
counted qs (k :: ks) woken = case OrdMap.lookup qs.waiting k of
  Just w ->
    counted
      (waitingIn k { w | left = w.left - 1 } qs)
      ks
      (if w.left == 1 then k :: woken else woken)
  Nothing -> abandon

-- (the behaviour gone from each of its parts, those waiting behind it
-- let in where they fit now: the queues after, and `woken` with those
-- to be woken)
leftAll : List (Pair Part Bool) -> Queues -> List Int -> Pair Queues (List Int)
leftAll Nil qs woken = MkPair qs woken
leftAll (MkPair p here :: rest) qs woken =
  let (sl, ks) = letIn (released (slotOf qs p) here) Nil
  in let (after, more) =
    counted (withSlot qs p sl (1 + List.length ks)) ks woken
  in leftAll rest after more

-- (the behaviour `k` watching the slot, or no longer, by `f`: on all of
-- it, or on a part inside it)
watchedAt : (Int -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit)
          -> Int
          -> Bool
          -> Slot
          -> Slot
watchedAt f k True sl = { sl | watchedHere = f k sl.watchedHere }
watchedAt f k False sl = { sl | watchedWithin = f k sl.watchedWithin }

-- (... each of its parts)
watchedBy : (Int -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit)
          -> Int
          -> List (Pair Part Bool)
          -> Queues
          -> Queues
watchedBy f k Nil qs = qs
watchedBy f k (MkPair p here :: rest) qs =
  watchedBy f k rest (withSlot qs p (watchedAt f k here (slotOf qs p)) 1)

watching : Int -> List (Pair Part Bool) -> Queues -> Queues
watching k nodes qs = watchedBy (\key m -> OrdMap.insert m key ()) k nodes qs

unwatched : Int -> List (Pair Part Bool) -> Queues -> Queues
unwatched k nodes qs = watchedBy (\key m -> OrdMap.delete m key) k nodes qs

-- (the keys of the map, among `ks`)
withKeys : OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit
         -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit
         -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit
withKeys ks m =
  List.foldl (\acc key -> OrdMap.insert acc key ()) ks (OrdMap.keys m)

-- (... those watching a part a behaviour wrote, all of it: on all of
-- it, on a part inside it, and on all of a part it is inside)
watchersAt : Queues -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit -> Part -> OrdMap.OrdMap Int Unit
watchersAt qs ks p =
  List.foldl
    (\acc q -> withKeys acc (slotOf qs q).watchedHere)
    (withKeys
       (withKeys ks (slotOf qs p).watchedHere)
       (slotOf qs p).watchedWithin)
    (enclosing p)

-- (those watching any part of `nodes` written: the parts for all of
-- which it was, a behaviour's cowns)
watchersOf : Queues -> List (Pair Part Bool) -> List Int
watchersOf qs nodes =
  OrdMap.keys
    (List.foldl
       (\acc n -> case n of
        MkPair p True -> watchersAt qs acc p
        MkPair p False -> acc)
       OrdMap.empty
       nodes)

-- (each of the behaviours `ks`, watching, woken by a write: no longer
-- watching, come to its parts' queues again, at the back, in the order
-- they were spawned; `woken` with those let in at once)
retried : List Int -> Queues -> List Int -> Pair Queues (List Int)
retried Nil qs woken = MkPair qs woken
retried (k :: ks) qs woken = case OrdMap.lookup qs.waiting k of
  Just w ->
    let (after, n) = joinedAll k w.nodes 0 (unwatched k w.nodes qs)
    in retried
      ks
      (waitingIn k { w | left = n } after)
      (if n == 0 then k :: woken else woken)
  Nothing -> abandon

-- (the behaviour `k` done, having written its cowns: gone from its
-- parts' queues, and those watching them come to the queues again)
done : Int -> Queues -> Pair Queues (List Int)
done k qs = case OrdMap.lookup qs.waiting k of
  Just w ->
    let (after, woken) =
      leftAll w.nodes { qs | waiting = OrdMap.delete qs.waiting k } Nil
    in retried (watchersOf after w.nodes) after woken
  Nothing -> abandon

-- (the behaviour `k` given up for now, having written nothing: gone
-- from its parts' queues, and watching them)
declined : Int -> Queues -> Pair Queues (List Int)
declined k qs = case OrdMap.lookup qs.waiting k of
  Just w ->
    let (after, woken) = leftAll w.nodes qs Nil
    in MkPair (watching k w.nodes after) woken
  Nothing -> abandon

-- Behaviours
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (each woken at its key)
wakeAll : {e : HFunctor} -> {{gr : green <: e}} -> List Int -> Co e Unit
wakeAll Nil = pure ()
wakeAll (ch :: rest) = do
  wake ch
  wakeAll rest

-- (waiting for its turn, unless it has come)
turn : {e : HFunctor} -> {{gr : green <: e}} -> Int -> Bool -> Co e Unit
turn ch True = pure ()
turn ch False = do
  park ch
  pure ()

-- (what the store holds)
nowOf : {s : Type} -> Behaviours s -> s
nowOf bs = bs.now

-- (behaviours left to run)
busy : {s : Type} -> Behaviours s -> Bool
busy bs = bs.live > 0

-- (... its queues `qs` now)
withQueues : {s : Type} -> Queues -> Behaviours s -> Behaviours s
withQueues qs bs = { bs | queues = qs }

-- (... and the channel `ch` waiting until none is)
idling : {s : Type} -> Int -> Behaviours s -> Behaviours s
idling ch bs = { bs | idle = ch :: bs.idle }

-- (... the behaviour on the key `ch`, on the cowns `c`, come to their
-- queues: whether its turn has come at once)
spawned : {s t : Type}
        -> Int
        -> Cown s t
        -> Behaviours s
        -> Pair (Behaviours s) Bool
spawned ch c bs =
  let (qs, ready) = queuedAs ch (nodesOf (parts c)) bs.queues
  in MkPair { bs | queues = qs, live = bs.live + 1 } ready

-- (... the behaviour on the key `ch` done, its cowns `c` holding `v`:
-- the state after, and whom to tell -- those whose turn it lets come,
-- and, where none is left, those waiting until then)
afterEnd : {s t : Type}
         -> Int
         -> Cown s t
         -> t
         -> Behaviours s
         -> Pair (Behaviours s) (List Int)
afterEnd ch c v bs =
  let (qs, woken) = done ch bs.queues
  in if bs.live == 1
  then MkPair
      { now = replaced c v bs.now, queues = qs, live = 0, idle = Nil }
      (woken ++ bs.idle)
  else MkPair
      { bs | now = replaced c v bs.now, queues = qs, live = bs.live - 1 }
      woken

-- (the behaviour on its key `ch` done, its cowns `c` holding `v`)
ended : {s t : Type}
      -> {e : HFunctor}
      -> {{gr : green <: e}}
      -> {{bc : boc s <: e}}
      -> Int
      -> Cown s t
      -> t
      -> Co e Unit
ended ch c v = do
  bs <- get (ev := bc)
  let (next, woken) = afterEnd ch c v bs
  put (ev := bc) next
  wakeAll woken

-- (the behaviour on its key `ch`, its condition false, its cowns let
-- go of, unwritten, until another writes one)
givenUp : {s : Type}
        -> {e : HFunctor}
        -> {{gr : green <: e}}
        -> {{bc : boc s <: e}}
        -> Int
        -> Co e Unit
givenUp ch = do
  bs <- get (ev := bc)
  let (qs, woken) = declined ch bs.queues
  put (ev := bc) (withQueues qs bs)
  wakeAll woken

-- (a behaviour, its turn come: where `cond` holds of what its cowns
-- hold, its body given that and what it gives back written; else its
-- cowns let go of, and its turn waited for again, which comes once
-- another behaviour has written one of them)
attempt : {s t : Type}
        -> {e : HFunctor}
        -> {{gr : green <: e}}
        -> {{bc : boc s <: e}}
        -> Int
        -> Cown s t
        -> (t -> Bool)
        -> (t -> Co e t)
        -> Co e Unit
attempt ch c cond body = do
  bs <- get (ev := bc)
  let v = contents c (nowOf bs)
  if cond v
  then do
    w <- body v
    ended ch c w
  else do
    givenUp (s := s) ch
    park ch
    attempt (bc := bc) ch c cond body

-- (a behaviour on the cowns at the position `c`, spawned, to run where
-- `cond` holds)
spawnedOn : {s t : Type}
          -> {e : HFunctor}
          -> {{gr : green <: e}}
          -> {{bc : boc s <: e}}
          -> Cown s t
          -> (t -> Bool)
          -> (t -> Co e t)
          -> Co e Unit
spawnedOn c cond body =
  if apart (parts c)
  then do
    ch <- newKey
    bs <- get (ev := bc)
    let (next, ready) = spawned ch c bs
    put (ev := bc) next
    spawn (do
      turn ch ready
      attempt ch c cond body)
  else abandon

-- | What a behaviour can be on, in a store of shape `s`: a cown, or a
-- | tuple of them (`(a, b, c)`, nesting to the left); what they hold,
-- | and the one position of it.
theory Cowns (c : Type) where
  Store : Type
  Contents : Type
  position : c -> Position Store Contents

-- | A cown: what it holds.
instance instanceCownsPosition : {s a : Type} -> Cowns (Position s a)
instanceCownsPosition = { Store = s, Contents = a, position = \c -> c }

-- | Two (each a cown or a tuple) of one store: the pair of what they
-- | hold.
instance instanceCownsPair : {c d : Type}
                           -> {{l : Cowns c}}
                           -> {{r : Cowns d @ { Store = l.Store }}}
                           -> Cowns (c, d)
instanceCownsPair =
  { Store = l.Store
  , Contents = (l.Contents, r.Contents)
  , position = \p -> both (l.position (fst p)) (r.position (snd p))
  }

-- | A behaviour on the cowns `cs`, one or a tuple of them, spawned;
-- | this one goes on.  Its turn comes once every behaviour spawned
-- | before it on any of them is done; then `body` is given what they
-- | hold, a tuple as `cs` is, and what it gives back is what they hold
-- | after.  Cowns that overlap are abandoned.
when : {c : Type}
     -> {e : HFunctor}
     -> c
     -> {{cw : Cowns c}}
     -> {{gr : green <: e}}
     -> {{bc : boc cw.Store <: e}}
     -> (cw.Contents -> Co e cw.Contents)
     -> Co e Unit
when cs body = spawnedOn (cw.position cs) (\v -> True) body

-- | A behaviour on the cowns `cs` that waits until `cond` holds of what
-- | they hold, spawned; this one goes on.  Its turn comes as a `when`'s
-- | does; where `cond` holds then, `body` runs as a `when`'s.  Where it
-- | does not, the behaviour lets its cowns go, writing nothing, and
-- | waits, taking no turn, until another behaviour has written one of
-- | them; then it comes to their queues again, at the back, before any
-- | spawned after that write, and tries again.  Where every behaviour
-- | left waits so, and none can write, `runBoc` says so (`Nothing`).
whenever : {c : Type}
         -> {e : HFunctor}
         -> c
         -> {{cw : Cowns c}}
         -> {{gr : green <: e}}
         -> {{bc : boc cw.Store <: e}}
         -> (cw.Contents -> Bool)
         -> (cw.Contents -> Co e cw.Contents)
         -> Co e Unit
whenever cs cond body = spawnedOn (cw.position cs) cond body

-- | Waiting until no behaviour is left to run: every one spawned, and
-- | every one they spawn, done.
drained : {s : Type}
        -> {e : HFunctor}
        -> {{gr : green <: e}}
        -> {{bc : boc s <: e}}
        -> Co e Unit
drained = do
  bs <- get (ev := bc)
  if busy bs
  then do
    ch <- newKey
    put (ev := bc) (idling ch bs)
    park ch
    drained (bc := bc)

-- (main's answer and the store at the end)
endOf : {s a : Type} -> (Maybe a, Behaviours s) -> Maybe (a, s)
endOf (Just x, bs) = Just (x, bs.now)
endOf (Nothing, bs) = Nothing

-- | `c` and the behaviours it spawns, on the store `st` and nothing
-- | else, in the language, the last of them waited for: main's answer
-- | and the store they leave, or `Nothing` where every thread waits --
-- | a behaviour holding its cowns while it waits for good, or every
-- | behaviour left a `whenever`'s waiting for a write none will make.
runBoc : {s a : Type}
       -> s
       -> ({e : HFunctor}
           -> {{gr : green <: e}}
           -> {{bc : boc s <: e}}
           -> Co e a)
       -> Maybe (a, s)
runBoc st c =
  endOf
    (greenWith
       (opening st) (do
     x <- c
     drained (s := s)
     pure x))
